A||||9||tgowens||Aluminum Flywheels||||1||
Z||000000||tgowens||09-06-2000||11:52 PM||||for those interested...here is a letter from a customer who is using our aluminum flywheel/kevlar clutch kit...<P>Hello all,<BR>   If anyone has thought about upgrading their Fiero 2.8L with an aluminum flywheel and<BR>wondered what the operating characteristics are you will want to read this:<P>   I need to let you all know about an awesome aluminum flywheel and kevlar clutch set by<BR>George Miller at the Fiero shop in California.   "George Miller The Fiero Shop"<BR>fieroshp@pacbell.net<P>  I put out a message to the list some time ago inquiring if anyone knew of a company which<BR>made the Aluminum flywheel for the 2.8L Fiero engine. Almost right away I got back many replies<BR>most expressing that it was a bad idea saying things like:<P>1.) " It won't be very streetable as the engine would have the tendency to want to slow down to<BR>quickly as a result of the weight reduction"<P>2.) " you will gain horses and loose torque, it's a trade off when you lighten the rotating<BR>mass" <P>3.) "I wouldn't trust an aluminum flywheel as it will wear out quickly, clutch against<BR>aluminum? don't try it!"   <BR>also I'll bet it arrives looking like two drunk monkeys hammered it out!"<P>4.) "It's only for the drag strip, you will have to rev the engine sooo high for any benefit,<BR>not a good street idea"<P>  And so on with the negatives.........<P>Answering #1 "I don't feel any dramatic slowing after I get off the accelerator, in fact I<BR>don't notice any difference slowing, decelerating at all."<P>Answering #2 "I understand about lightening and loosing torque, this aluminum flywheel weighed<BR>in at exactly 7 LBS.<BR>I also weighed my stock flywheel which weighed in at exactly 14LBS. 8OZ. I was initially<BR>concerned here but after the install".............. (see below)<P>Answering #3 "when the aluminum flywheel arrived it was absolutely beautiful, machined<BR>perfectly and as for aluminum against clutch material. It is inlaid with a metal ring at the<BR>clutch contact point so this is what the clutch material makes contact with. no premature<BR>wearing will occur......also "Superb machining"<P>Answering #4 "True that this idea is used on the strip and I can certainly see why. Untrue, I<BR>do not have to rev the engine like they do on the strip, although if I did I'd have a tiger by<BR>the tail!" Very streetable, nothing negative to report here folks.......       <BR>______________________________________________________ <BR>So among all the negative chat:<BR>Then George Miller from the Fiero Shop dropped me a line I called him and he cut me a great<BR>deal for a what he called a "prototype" flywheel and kevlar kit for my Fiero. I had already<BR>made a purchase of a Center force clutch set but decided to send it back and purchased his<BR>complete clutch set.<BR>So I took him up on the deal and I'm here to tell you all that this is a wonderful modification<BR>to do with your 2.8L rides!<P>After the install:<BR>You will definitely feel this mod in the seat of the pants! The car can be driven normally the<BR>weight reduction only shows itself if you need it.  But when you choose to accelerate<BR>aggressively, WOW, hang on!! You will notice an immediate performance increase with half the<BR>weight of a stock flywheel. If you are accelerating aggressively you will be able to shift<BR>"very quickly" through the gears as the car reacts immediately to throttle position spooling up<BR>very quickly! Frankly I don't feel any torque loss only gains felt with this set from George<BR>Miller.<BR>Again, the car can be driven normally the aluminum flywheels aren't only for the strip.<P>"Please contact George, not me about price, I'm sure that he will beat all others for the<BR>aluminum flywheel and kevlar clutch set."<P>"Thank you George, for this wonderful modification!"<P>Mike (in Delaware)<BR>"Happy customer" <P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/Terry_sig.gif">                    <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A><BR>Gold '87 GT<BR>Blue '87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shaun41178||09-07-2000||01:20 PM||||Thanks for the info.  I myslef own an auto tranny but i am sure this info will benefit many manual tranny fiero owners when thinking of going to a lighter flywheel or not.  i hope Hyptnotise sees this.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000002||loafer87gt||09-07-2000||01:30 PM||||This sounds very cool. Do you know if a lightened flywheel puts any extra stress on your clutch or tranny? Do you need to have a special kind of clutch, or will the factory GM/Luc clutch work? Also, I'm assuming you have to have your engine internally balanced to do this mod, right?||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||09-07-2000||01:52 PM||||loafer87gt, as to your first question, the answer is this flywheel puts no stress on the your tranny or axles anymore then the stock flywheel. <BR>Answer 2: The stock clutch will work but we recomend our kevlar clutch as this flywheel is designed to work better with it.<BR>Answer 3: As far as internnally balanced engine we have both sets of flywheels so that you can either use an internnally balanced eng. or the stock engine depending on what you have.<P>------------------<BR> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||HYPTNOTiSE||09-07-2000||08:56 PM||||How much for an internally balanced flywheel,, i already have the clutch setup with a kevlar fiber disk and valeo pressure plate.  Give me a good deal, i'm going to be putting my engine and tranny back together soon, i'd like to have one, my cars going to be really fast.<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||09-07-2000||09:24 PM||||Can I get one with a custom bolt pattern? I need one to fit a 4.9 Cadillac. I can supply the measurements for the crank pattern, the rest can be '88 Fiero spec. (nuetral balance).||||reg||5
Z||000006||fieroshop||09-08-2000||04:44 AM||||HYPTNOTiSE, our flywheels are sold complete as a set with the clutch, throwout bearing and pressure plate.<P>------------------<BR> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||HYPTNOTiSE||09-08-2000||02:16 PM||||Why would you not want to sell the flywheel? I dont want the clutch, i already spend good money on that. Sell me a flywheel, it's all I want.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fieroshop||09-09-2000||02:03 AM||||we have found that some clutches on the market tend to destroy a flywheel. We have found that the kevlar clutch actually polishes the flywheel rather than destroying it. Everything we sell has a warranty on it but if we don't know the type of clutch to be used with the flywheel it makes it difficult to warranty the flywheel. For that reason we elected to sell the set-up as a package rather than separately.||||reg||1
Z||000009||HYPTNOTiSE||09-09-2000||02:09 AM||||is your fiber disk fiber pucks on both sides or is one side organic?<BR>||||reg||1
